> Invis / see invis as early as possible

I'd guess less than 5% of my characters have invisibility at
ascension, and I consider see invis to be borderline useless.  Once in
a while it's nice, but it's pretty freaking rare that you find any
invisible monster that's an actual thread.

> Have MR before going deep in the dungeon or mines end

MR before DL8 (where polytraps start appearing) is quite nice.  And MR
is one of the handful of nearly must-have intrinsics for the full
game.

> But the one I want to ask about is teleportitis + intrinsic teleport
> control.

These are incredibly useful for playing a fun and fast game, but
they're not "must have" in terms of survival.  I certainly rate them
as far, far more important than invisibilty or see invisible.

MR, reflection, poison res are the "big 3" in my mind, along with
sufficiently low AC/high HP (those 2 trade off of each other) and
having at least 1 "Elbereth out" (a wand of fire/lightining/digging/
etc or an athame or something) and 1 non-Elberth "out" (level teleport
or ?earth or whatever).


Things like jumping, telecontrol, conflict, hunger, any halfway decent
weapon, a !full healing, ESP, "oLS, etc are next on the list.


